Let me look at the project structure to understand how to run both services.

Listed directory ARAS
Listed directory backend
Viewed run.py:1-14
Listed directory frontend
Viewed start.bat:1-96

You already have a `start.bat` script in the project root. Just run it:

```
e:\PROJECTS\ARAS\start.bat
```

This will open **two separate command windows**:

| Service | URL | Port |
|---------|-----|------|
| **Backend** (FastAPI/Uvicorn) | http://localhost:2022 | 2022 |
| **Frontend** (Vite dev server) | http://localhost:3033 | 3033 |
| **API Docs** | http://localhost:2022/docs | — |

### Or run them manually in two terminals:

**Terminal 1 — Backend:**
```powershell
cd e:\PROJECTS\ARAS\backend
.\venv\Scripts\activate
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 2022
```

**Terminal 2 — Frontend:**
```powershell
cd e:\PROJECTS\ARAS\frontend
npm run dev
```

